{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "25616848",
      "title": "Preparing Paths with \"getStaticPaths\" & Working With Fallback Pages",
      "sourceHash": "5802516d5ee1eb89279a56f19c632cc7c21cee3d011ef9ea2039126a7b0adce1",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.427,
          "end": 3.72,
          "en": "getStaticPaths",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.72,
          "end": 5.331,
          "en": "is another function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.331,
          "end": 6.914,
          "en": "NextJS understands,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 8.49,
          "end": 10.275,
          "en": "just like getStaticProps",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 10.275,
          "end": 12.357,
          "en": "and getServerSideProps.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 12.357,
          "end": 16.173,
          "en": "And getStaticPaths is a function you need to export",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 16.173,
          "end": 18.88,
          "en": "in a page component file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 18.88,
          "end": 21.511,
          "en": "If it's a dynamic page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 21.511,
          "end": 26.013,
          "en": "like we have it here and you're using getStaticProps,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 26.013,
          "end": 28.972,
          "en": "not if you're using getServerSideProps",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 28.972,
          "end": 32.077,
          "en": "and not if you're using neever get static",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 32.077,
          "end": 33.7,
          "en": "nor getServerSideProps",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 33.7,
          "end": 38,
          "en": "but it is needed if you do use getStaticProps.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 38,
          "end": 42.23,
          "en": "So in that case, you need to export another function here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 42.23,
          "end": 44.56,
          "en": "in this page component file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 44.56,
          "end": 48.3,
          "en": "And that's the getStaticPaths function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 48.3,
          "end": 50.9,
          "en": "And this can also be a async function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 50.9,
          "end": 54.61,
          "en": "so that you can use a single weight in there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 54.61,
          "end": 58.42,
          "en": "Now what's the deal with getStaticPaths though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 58.42,
          "end": 61.93,
          "en": "To understand it, let's again think about the fact",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 61.93,
          "end": 64.11,
          "en": "that with getStaticProps",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 64.11,
          "end": 68.49,
          "en": "a page is pre-generated during the build process.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 68.49,
          "end": 70.28,
          "en": "Now, what does this mean?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 70.28,
          "end": 75.28,
          "en": "This means that of course, NextJS needs to pre-generate",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 75.62,
          "end": 80.03,
          "en": "all versions of this dynamic page in advance",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 80.03,
          "end": 82.9,
          "en": "for all the supported IDs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 82.9,
          "end": 86.89,
          "en": "Because since this is dynamic, NextJS needs to know",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 86.89,
          "end": 91.22,
          "en": "for which ID values it should pre-generate the page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 91.22,
          "end": 95.13,
          "en": "Because how would it pre-generate this page otherwise?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 95.13,
          "end": 98.75,
          "en": "We get the ID from the URL here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 98.75,
          "end": 102.22999999999999,
          "en": "Great, but keep in mind that this is not pre-generated",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 102.22999999999999,
          "end": 105.43,
          "en": "when a user visits this page with a specific value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 105.43,
          "end": 109.12,
          "en": "in the URL, but during the build process.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 109.12,
          "end": 113.66,
          "en": "So here we need to pre-generated for all the URLs,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 113.66,
          "end": 117.89,
          "en": "for all the meetup ID values users might be entering",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 117.89,
          "end": 119.71000000000001,
          "en": "at runtime.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 119.71000000000001,
          "end": 123.03,
          "en": "And if they enter an ID for which we didn't pre-generate",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 123.03,
          "end": 126.57,
          "en": "the page, they will see a 404 error.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 126.57,
          "end": 128.74,
          "en": "But because that is how it works,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 128.74,
          "end": 131.26,
          "en": "we need to add getStaticPaths",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 131.26,
          "end": 133.889,
          "en": "which has the job of returning an object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 133.889,
          "end": 138.82,
          "en": "where we describe all the dynamic segment values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 138.82,
          "end": 141.14,
          "en": "So all the meetup IDs in this case,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 141.14,
          "end": 144.53300000000002,
          "en": "for which this page should be pre-generated.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 145.51,
          "end": 148.7,
          "en": "Now for this, this object needs to have a paths key,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 148.7,
          "end": 150.2,
          "en": "which is an array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 150.2,
          "end": 153.02,
          "en": "And in that array, you must have multiple objects",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 153.02,
          "end": 157.35,
          "en": "one object per version of this dynamic page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 157.35,
          "end": 159.7,
          "en": "Where this object has a parans key.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 159.7,
          "end": 163.8,
          "en": "That's a must have, which then itself again is an object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 163.8,
          "end": 165.54,
          "en": "with all the key value pairs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 165.54,
          "end": 167.81,
          "en": "that might lead to your dynamic page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 167.81,
          "end": 170.75,
          "en": "So if you have multiple dynamic segments,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 170.75,
          "end": 174.88,
          "en": "then you would have multiple keys in this nested object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 174.88,
          "end": 179.32,
          "en": "Here we only have meetup ID as a single dynamic segment.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 179.32,
          "end": 181.46,
          "en": "And hence here in this parans object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 181.46,
          "end": 183.49,
          "en": "we would add a meetup ID key",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 183.49,
          "end": 187.33,
          "en": "and then enter the concrete value for meetup ID",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 187.33,
          "end": 190.48,
          "en": "for which this page should be pre-generated.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 190.48,
          "end": 193.03,
          "en": "And if we have multiple possible values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 193.03,
          "end": 196.07,
          "en": "Like in this case where I have, M1 and M2",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 196.07,
          "end": 201.07,
          "en": "we would return a paths array with two objects inside of it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 201.07,
          "end": 204.723,
          "en": "where the other one uses M2 as a meetup ID.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 206.07,
          "end": 209.47,
          "en": "Now, in reality, you would of course not hard-code this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 209.47,
          "end": 210.67000000000002,
          "en": "as a developer,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 210.67000000000002,
          "end": 214.37,
          "en": "but you would also fetch your supported IDs from a database",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 214.37,
          "end": 218.91,
          "en": "or from an API and generate this array dynamically.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 218.91,
          "end": 221.5,
          "en": "And we are also going to do that later,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 221.5,
          "end": 223.803,
          "en": "but for the moment let's hard-code it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 225.03,
          "end": 228.68,
          "en": "With that, if you save that file with getStaticPaths added",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 228.68,
          "end": 232.01,
          "en": "with this code and with getStaticProps",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 232.01,
          "end": 235.40699999999998,
          "en": "still being in there, with that if you now reload,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 235.40699999999998,
          "end": 237.69,
          "en": "we don't get this error anymore.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 237.69,
          "end": 241.72,
          "en": "Instead we get this error regarding the fallback key",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 241.72,
          "end": 244.38,
          "en": "instead of getStaticPaths.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 244.38,
          "end": 246.53,
          "en": "And that's another piece of configuration,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 246.53,
          "end": 249.55,
          "en": "which you need to add in this returned object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 249.55,
          "end": 252.02,
          "en": "next to your paths key,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 252.02,
          "end": 254.42,
          "en": "the fallback key.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 254.42,
          "end": 258.92,
          "en": "This key tells NextJS whether your paths array",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 258.92,
          "end": 262.43,
          "en": "contains all supported parameter values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 262.43,
          "end": 264.85,
          "en": "or just some of them.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 264.85,
          "end": 268.31,
          "en": "If you set fall back to false,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 268.31,
          "end": 269.81,
          "en": "you say that your paths",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 269.81,
          "end": 273.8,
          "en": "contains all supported meetup ID values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 273.8,
          "end": 276.34000000000003,
          "en": "That means that if the user enters anything",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 276.34000000000003,
          "end": 278.89,
          "en": "that's not supported here, for example, M3",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 280.034,
          "end": 283.47,
          "en": "he or she would see a 404 error.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 283.47,
          "end": 286.1,
          "en": "If you set fall back to true on the other hand,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 286.1,
          "end": 288.83,
          "en": "NextJS would try to generate a page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 288.83,
          "end": 292.047,
          "en": "for this meetup ID dynamically on the server",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 292.047,
          "end": 293.473,
          "en": "for the incoming request.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 294.35,
          "end": 296.09000000000003,
          "en": "Fall back is a nice feature",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 296.09000000000003,
          "end": 299.99,
          "en": "because it allows you to pre-generate some of your pages",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 299.99,
          "end": 302.9,
          "en": "for specific meetup ID values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 302.9,
          "end": 307.17,
          "en": "For example the pages which are visited most frequently",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 307.17,
          "end": 310.36,
          "en": "and then pre-generate the missing ones dynamically",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 310.36,
          "end": 313.023,
          "en": "when requests for them are coming in.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 313.86,
          "end": 316.52,
          "en": "Here however, I'll set fallback to false",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 316.52,
          "end": 321.5,
          "en": "to indicate that I defined all supported paths here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 321.5,
          "end": 324.14,
          "en": "Now, if you wanna learn more about fallback and so on,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 324.14,
          "end": 327.63,
          "en": "I do cover that in greater detail in my full course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 327.63,
          "end": 328.98,
          "en": "But the general concept",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 328.98,
          "end": 331.57,
          "en": "is that we can simply define some paths",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 331.57,
          "end": 333.24,
          "en": "instead of all paths.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 333.24,
          "end": 335.75,
          "en": "If we, for example, have hundreds of pages",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 335.75,
          "end": 338.48,
          "en": "and we don't wanna pre-generate all of them,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 338.48,
          "end": 341.14300000000003,
          "en": "but maybe just our most popular pages.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 342.09000000000003,
          "end": 344.58,
          "en": "And therefore with fallback added now,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 344.58,
          "end": 346.63,
          "en": "if we save this again and reload,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 346.63,
          "end": 351.01,
          "en": "now we successfully load the page for this first meetup.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 351.01,
          "end": 353.72,
          "en": "If I go to M2, that also works.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 353.72,
          "end": 357.61,
          "en": "But if I enter M3, I get the default 404 page here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 357.61,
          "end": 360.47,
          "en": "because I had fallback set to false",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 360.47,
          "end": 364.483,
          "en": "and M3 is not one of the supported parameters here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 365.48,
          "end": 367.614,
          "en": "That's how this works.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 367.614,
          "end": 368.487,
          "en": "And getStaticPaths",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 368.487,
          "end": 371.16,
          "en": "therefore is another important function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 371.16,
          "end": 375.05,
          "en": "which you need in dynamic pages to tell NextJS",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 375.05,
          "end": 377.564,
          "en": "for which dynamic parameter values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 377.564,
          "end": 380.57,
          "en": "this page should be pre-generated.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 380.57,
          "end": 384.36,
          "en": "And then again, getStaticProps executes for every page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 384.36,
          "end": 388.07,
          "en": "So for every meetup ID value allows you to fetch data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 388.07,
          "end": 390.93,
          "en": "for that meetup and allows you to return props",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 390.93,
          "end": 392.54,
          "en": "for that meetup.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 392.54,
          "end": 395.96,
          "en": "And as a side note here, where I locked the meetup ID",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 395.96,
          "end": 399.01,
          "en": "we do see that here in this terminal.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 399.01,
          "end": 401.68,
          "en": "We don't see it in the browser,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 401.68,
          "end": 402.90999999999997,
          "en": "developer tools,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 402.90999999999997,
          "end": 404.79,
          "en": "here the console is empty",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 404.79,
          "end": 408.93,
          "en": "because I mentioned that this is called the code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 408.93,
          "end": 412.57,
          "en": "instead of getStaticProps, which runs during build time.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 412.57,
          "end": 414.77,
          "en": "And when running in the development server",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 414.77,
          "end": 417.44,
          "en": "it does run for every incoming request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 135,
          "start": 417.44,
